 +| 11.11 | **Board item 10: "where did the effects and lighting go".** Nothing was lost in git: `render/lookdev`, `claude/lookdev` and `claude/audio-vfx-wiring` are all merged into main. Two runtime causes. (a) The frame-time governor (render/quality.js) watched the first 40 s of the session, which is now the town with its model streaming; on the owner's RTX 2060 SUPER (detected `high`) the loading hitches pushed it to `low`, which renders without the post stack (bloom, GTAO, grading, grain) and without the lamp lights, and with a flat cloud deck. Fix: on desktop a GPU detected as `high` or `ultra` never drops below `high` on its own (`governorFloor`); phones and weak desktops keep the full range. (b) The settings' Quality (auto/high/low) never reached the 3D tier: `tierForPreference` existed but was not called. Fix: boot-world reads the preference at start and on change; a fixed choice switches the governor off. Still true and not changed: the named VFX module (src/vfx, Shell mist, crack pulse, tension, glyph sign) is created only when the season starts at the Tournament altar, so the town shows the look-dev atmosphere but none of those effects. Checks: `npm test` green, 643 (one more governor-floor case in tests/client/quality.test.mjs); not measured on the owner's PC (the GPU server is an RTX 4090, which never trips the governor). |
